   "etapa": "explicar",
   "piezas": [
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Because, and then",
     "texto": [
      "To join two sentences with «because», **-아/어서** is used on the first verb. What follows is the result.",
      "피곤하다 → **피곤해서** (because I'm tired). 가다 → **가서** (went and…).",
      "피곤**해서** 집에 갔어요 = because I was tired, I went home."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Order of the ideas",
     "texto": [
      "In Korean the cause comes first and the result after, as in English.",
      "You already know **아파서** (because I'm ill) from A1; now it is used with any verb or adjective."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
